{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition","id":272992,"title":"Why a Second Edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-05T09:51:10-07:00","id":272992,"title":"Why a Second Edition?","content":"This is not a negative post or the start of an edition wars.<br /> <br /> I'm seriously asking...what has changed with the game so much that a second edition seems necessary?<br /> <br /> I have the same questions regarding Promethean and Scion.<br /> <br /> I understand why some other games have been reimagined. For example, Demon the Descent is a totally new take on the oWoD Demon the Fallen. So I see where you need a new book and line for that product.<br /> <br /> But are Promethean, Aberrant/Adventure/Trinity, and Scion changing scope to the degree that Demon did (love the new Demon by the way) or is this just a fiddling with the rules tweak and the fluff is still the same?<br /> <br /> I'm just trying to decide how far down the rabbit hole of new editions I can go. If the various Second Editions are totally new directions for the property, then I'll have to look at picking them up. If they are just rules tweaks, then I'm probably good with what I've got...and I've got just about everything from those three (five) properties.<br /> <br /> Thanks for any insight into &quot;why a second edition&quot;.<br /> <br /> =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","user":"MidnightBlue","date":". 10-05-2014, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T10:15:25-07:00","id":273027,"title":"","content":"It's been ten years since the New World of Darkness started.<br /> <br /> Demon: the Descent is not a second edition of Demon: the Fallen - it's a separate game in the same fashion as Vampire: the Requiem, Werewolf: the Forsaken, and Mage: the Awakening are separate games from Vampire: the Masquerade, Werewolf: the Apocalypse, and Mage: the Ascension, respectively.<br /> <br /> Promethean's second edition is more akin to <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/123898/Blood-and-Smoke-The-Strix-Chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle</a>, which is functionally and soon textually going to be Vampire: the Requiem Second Edition.<br /> <br /> In short, a second edition because the games have evolved over time and ten years is quite long enough to justify refining the material's presentation and incorporating <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">mechanical adjustments.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Mage: the Awakening is not a different game from Mage: the Awakening. 11-20-2014, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T10:51:40-07:00","id":273057,"title":"","content":"Well, we're getting mortal-level play, ten core pantheons, and the opportunity to play non-Scion supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Scion's mechanics were infamously broken, and really couldn't handle the power scaling the game called for, so they've been spending considerable time on a new Storyteller-inspired system that can handle scaling better.<br /> <br /> Then there's the opportunity to include more accurate research (most notable with the Loa/Yoruba, but most of the pantheons need it to a greater or lesser extent), to provide rules for PCs to create their own pantheons, for PCs to adopt other divine identities, and thereby alternate powersets...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T10:57:22-07:00","id":273061,"title":"","content":"Hi. The various developers can tell you more about the specific changes in the second editions, but I can give a broad overview.<br /> <br /> In <i>Promethean, </i>there's a lot changing, although it's not a <i>Fallen</i> to <i>Descent</i> jump. The setting is being renovated to make it more accessible and more exciting, including expanding the roster of splats. Powers have been redesigned from scratch, going even further than in <i>Vampire</i>'s second edition, <i>Blood and Smoke</i>. It's being built on the second edition nWoD rules, first seen in <i>The God-Machine Chronicle</i>.<br /> <br /> In <i>Scion</i>, the game is being expanded to include a &quot;street-level&quot; power tier and multiple variations on the core setting. The treatment of several pantheons is being overhauled: for example, the Mesoamerican pantheons are getting a more authentic portrayal. The rules are new from the ground up, since there were a lot of issues with the first edition mechanics and powers. We're taking an improved (and entirely different) approach to the scaling from mortal to god.<br /> <br /> In <i>Trinity</i>, the setting is being evolved in a number of ways, including introducing a modern day (pre-<i>Aberrant</i>) branch of the universe with its own organizations and history that tie into the larger chronology. I'll defer to Ian, the lead developer, on a more detailed explanation. It's also using the same new rules as <i>Scion</i>.<br /> <br /> All of these second editions include significant setting additions, and the rules changes go beyond tweaks and bug fixes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T11:21:10-07:00","id":273095,"title":"","content":"Even if we changed virtually nothing in the setting and mechanics, it wouldn't be fair if we started releasing new material for a game, but required people to buy/own a rulebook released 15 or more years ago in order to play it. Those original rulebooks are often hard to find or prohibitively expensive or both.<br /> <br /> It makes a lot more sense to release new rulebooks, especially considering that we are changing both the setting and system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T12:56:20-07:00","id":273168,"title":"","content":"What rules will you use for Trinity? Will it be the rules version from GMC? Will there be conditions and beats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","name":"dailor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T14:22:56-07:00","id":273223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dailor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=273168#post273168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What rules will you use for Trinity? Will it be the rules version from GMC? Will there be conditions and beats?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its a new OPP system. Read collected notes about what fans know of the new Trinity Continuum games / system so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ayGNCnAsHcgxIUr9k6mNYf46loqY8Qlv5v4TIImqgdU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum: What We Know</a><br /> <br /> Hope that helps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T15:06:00-07:00","id":273238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=273095#post273095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if we changed virtually nothing in the setting and mechanics, it wouldn't be fair if we started releasing new material for a game, but required people to buy/own a rulebook released 15 or more years ago in order to play it. Those original rulebooks are often hard to find or prohibitively expensive or both.<br /> <br /> It makes a lot more sense to release new rulebooks, especially considering that we are changing both the setting and system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My only argument with this is that out of print books can be reprinted.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the comments all. I never want to be &quot;that guy&quot; afraid of a new edition, and I've seen plenty of games that were helped by new editions. Maybe I just don't play enough Storyteller these days to see the difference. But in the years of playing Aberrant and most of the oWoD and in buying and reading huge chunks of the nWoD and Scion, I guess I don't see all that much of a change in the Storyteller system over the years. I'm sure I'm missing some nuance between the lines.<br /> <br /> I've always loved the fluff of the Storyteller games which is why I have two and a half book cases devoted to those books. As I said, I'm just not sure how many more times I can buy all of the books again...especially if having the new hotness makes my prior collection obsolete. And that would be a crime as there are some amazing reads there.<br /> <br /> Well, I'll reserve any opinions until I see one of them in the flesh.<br /> <br /> Thanks again, all.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T15:15:31-07:00","id":273239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=273027#post273027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been ten years since the New World of Darkness started.<br /> <br /> Demon: the Descent is not a second edition of Demon: the Fallen - it's a separate game in the same fashion as Vampire: the Requiem, Werewolf: the Forsaken, and Mage: the Awakening are separate games from Vampire: the Masquerade, Werewolf: the Apocalypse, and Mage: the Awakening, respectively.<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">mechanical adjustments.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I said. I can see why there are two separate lines for Demon: The Fallen and Demon: The Descent as they aren't edition changes but totally different takes on the idea of a Demonic-centric game. =)<br /> <br /> <br /> Man...I'd have loved to see Adventure!, Aberrant, and Trinity get some more lovin' to go along with the nearly complete collection I already have. We had a lot of fun in those games. Even with suffering our usual Gaming ADD with all the options out there, our regular Friday night group played Aberrant straight for over a year. No other game has that honor.<br /> <br /> Adventure! never did get the attention it deserved with just the one book. =(<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T15:33:16-07:00","id":273260,"title":"","content":"I would also like to add that this trend in rewriting what has already been written does make me a little gunshy about buying less current books. The only core nWoD books I don't have are Changeling the Lost and Geist and I was considering picking them up when the finances opened up again after some Kickstarter depletion. There are more than a few books from some of the other lines that I was considering too. However it is starting to seem like maybe I should just hold off. Another couple of years down the road and they'll likely be redone.<br /> <br /> But I'm sure that's just me and needing to decide where my stretched funding will go.<br /> <br /> Huh...actually I think Changeling the Lost and Geist are THE only core White-Wolf/Onyx Path books I don't have (save old editions of oWoD that I got rid of when I &quot;upgraded&quot; and the 20th Anniversary editions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","user":"MidnightBlue","date":". 10-05-2014, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T15:53:12-07:00","id":273273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MidnightBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=273238#post273238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My only argument with this is that out of print books can be reprinted.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the best of my knowledge, we don't have most of the necessary files from 17 years ago to issue a reprint, or we'd have PoD options available already. The amount of time it would take to redesign and layout the exact same book could be put to better use designing and layout out something new.<br /> <br /> We don't want to do the same thing that was done almost 20 years ago. The industry has changed, the people have changed, times have changed, and this is a different company. We're doing something new.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But in the years of playing Aberrant and most of the oWoD and in buying and reading huge chunks of the nWoD and Scion, I guess I don't see all that much of a change in the Storyteller system over the years. </div> </div> </div>There's been considerable amount of change over the years. &quot;Difficulty&quot; doesn't even mean the same thing between Classic WoD and TU/Exalted.<br /> <br /> Irrelevant anyway, because as mentioned, we're creating a new system. It's not Storyteller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've always loved the fluff of the Storyteller games which is why I have two and a half book cases devoted to those books. As I said, I'm just not sure how many more times I can buy all of the books again...especially if having the new hotness makes my prior collection obsolete. And that would be a crime as there are some amazing reads there. </div> </div> </div>This has always been the case. Almost since RPGs were first invented in the 1970s, there have been new editions. Vampire: The Masquerade had three editions over the course of 7 years. It's been 17 since Aeon was first published. That's an extremely long time between editions. It's about time for something new, and that's what we're delivering.<br /> <br /> Old material is as obsolete as you want to make it. You could discard it entirely, sure, or you could mine it for ideas and continue to use it. Or you could continue to play in the old system. No one's holding a gun to your head.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T18:22:18-07:00","id":273375,"title":"","content":"I feel the pain of having to buy a whole set of books again, but new editions are a good thing. Mechanics evolve and the world keeps on spinning. It's especially important for science-fiction games where the &quot;Gee, someday tech might be able to this!&quot; turns into &quot;Tech has been able to do that for years now!&quot; I loved Shadowrun 2nd Edition, but after a while it gets silly that people are running around with keyboard sized computer that require hard-line internet access when we can do better than that real world. <br /> <br /> It's been 17 years. That's a long time to get life out of a book. I was in middle school when these games came out; I still have my books. I want an update. I want them to have a chance to fix the mistakes we made the first time around, and update the setting. I'm ready. It's an exciting time, and a chance to see new material for a game at long last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T08:40:28-07:00","id":273891,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Like I said, it wasn't a &quot;which is better&quot; discussion. I really was just trying to gauge if we were talking rules change, setting change, or both.<br /> <br /> But the argument that, &quot;It's been X years since the book came out so we need to make a new one,&quot; does rub me a little wrong. <br /> <br /> The classics never die...well...until someone stops printing the books and they become impossible to grab. =)<br /> <br /> I can understand having a new vision for a concept and wanting to make a new game to take the game to new places.<br /> <br /> I can understand trying to alter the feel of a game with new mechanics.<br /> <br /> But I never really understood the notion that if something hasn't been altered in 5, 10, 20, or even 30+ years, then it is outdated.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 1E doesn't really do it for me, it never really did after I discovered more free form advancement and build systems, but it sure seems to work well for others...even after all these years.<br /> <br /> I'll have to keep my eye on the progress of these three games/settings and see if I'll jump in. I HAVE to stop somewhere and just enjoy what I have. A new supplement can build on existing campaigns...even years and decades old. A new system might allow for a conversion, but sometimes is just far too much trouble than it is worth. But that's something that I'll need to evaluate on my own side of the screen.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the insight all.<br /> <br /> =)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T11:14:04-07:00","id":274050,"title":"","content":"It isn't that a game spoils after x years, it's that it is hard to argue that you are being ripped-off when you have had two decades to get play out of the game.<br /> <br /> *games DO spoil and become outdated though; advancements in science, technology, history and cultural understanding happen at a regular enough intervals to render a game laughable, pointless, or even offensive without at least occasional updates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T12:24:49-07:00","id":274093,"title":"","content":"I beg to differ. Games _may_ spoil. But that isn't necessarily the case. Just as new editions of a game aren't necessarily better than the original. I'd say Trinity aged pretty well. Many problems I had with the early story teller games have been done with and setting wise everything seems still fresh. Compare with Star Frontiers for example. You'lll have a good laugh. But I still prefer D&amp;D BECMI from the early 80s over any later edition and play it even today after so many years. Outdated? Maybe. Spoiled? Never!<br /> <br /> That being said I fully understand Onyx Path. There is a new team with new people and new ideas. Of course they'll have a different approach to the game. I'd be disappointed if they didn't. I just ask so I know if I (personally) am on board of that train or not. I didn't like the system changes of GMC, so this is my first concern. But even if I don't like the way Trinity will change, I still have the original and maybe new customers will hop aboard the new Trinity and find their playstyle supported.<br /> <br /> There is no perfect one-size-fits-all gaming system. And there will never be one. Sometimes I like the way things go, sometimes I don't. But that has nothing to do with the quality of a system or its creators. We all in this thread will have fun with Trinity. Some with the old edition, some with the new.<br /> <br /> Of course one may dream of the old edition being available on drivethru as print on demand or something like that. But I might as well ask for world peace. Or a light sabre. Sigh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1138-dailor","name":"dailor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T13:32:14-07:00","id":274141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=274050#post274050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't that a game spoils after x years, it's that it is hard to argue that you are being ripped-off when you have had two decades to get play out of the game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Heh...well, I never claimed to being ripped off. So that was never a concern of mine.<br /> <br /> =)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T13:34:05-07:00","id":274142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dailor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=274093#post274093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I might as well ask for world peace. Or a light sabre. Sigh</div> </div> </div> </div>World peace or lightsaber...world peace or lightsaber.<br /> <br /> Tough, tough call.<br /> <br /> =)<br /> <br /> <br /> But that is another case in point. I hear great things about Fantasy Flight's Star Wars game...and I'm HUGE Star Wars fan. However, I've got all but three or so books for West End Games' Star Wars (my favorite) and most of the books for the D20 and Saga editions of WotC's Star Wars.<br /> <br /> I just can't bring myself to buy another right now...no matter how good it might be.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","user":"MidnightBlue","date":". 10-06-2014, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T11:08:28-07:00","id":275578,"title":"","content":"They're making new editions for lots of reasons that have been mentioned. Another reason is that they're artists, of a sort, and it's been about 15 years since they've made art on this subject. They want to be creative and bring new art into the world, so they're making new art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T12:54:48-07:00","id":276592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MidnightBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=273260#post273260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also like to add that this trend in rewriting what has already been written does make me a little gunshy about buying less current books. The only core nWoD books I don't have are Changeling the Lost and Geist and I was considering picking them up when the finances opened up again after some Kickstarter depletion. There are more than a few books from some of the other lines that I was considering too. However it is starting to seem like maybe I should just hold off. Another couple of years down the road and they'll likely be redone.</div> </div> </div> </div>A second edition of CtL is already in the works, actually, so that's probably a good call.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T23:16:40-07:00","id":281989,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't actually play most of the other games but I can respond to the Scion question of why a new edition.<br /> <br /> First, and likely the most important being that Scion as it is, was made as a limited game, they never intended it to go past the first 3 books but added the 2 additional books (Companion and Ragnarok) due to overwhelming fan interest....and I can only assume the Yazata file was put together for the same reason, though if you look through it the meat of it was the important part to get out as unlike the other books, they spent exactly 0 hours on the art (Look through the other books and you'll find that, unless I missed something, every single picture in that file is from another book). It is a new company that is starting over and are, I am assuming here, looking to expand past the limited line into the ability to continue the game further on down the road. So in all honesty instead of looking at it as a 2nd Edition, you can really look at it as a Remake. <br /> <br /> Second, as said in other posts, the scaling for the game is kinda broken. They are also missing things like decent crafting rules for someone who actually wants to play a god of crafting, some rather iconic weapons and armor for various pantheons (Seriously....who the hell doesn't put stats for the most widely recognized armor in the whole of the Roman Empire in the book when you have the Dodekatheon as a Pantheon...that one irritates me more than it should but screw it *L*), and a number of other tiny things that could just really benefit from being well rounded out.<br /> <br /> Third, as said earlier they are also including rules for playing some &quot;Lower Level&quot; type characters, non-scions, pre-visitation scions and whatnot (Who here hasn't been wondering what it'd be like to play a Sorcerer or a Tengu in a Scion setting?). <br /> <br /> Fourth, and this one is just speculation here but with all the added space in the books, perhaps along with the revamping of the Pantheons, giving them a nice new polish and whatnot they'll be including more gods in the list (Sekhmet, Thanatos, Hathor, Eris ect ect)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T23:19:54-07:00","id":281991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=281989#post281989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't actually play most of the other games but I can respond to the Scion question of why a new edition.<br /> <br /> First, and likely the most important being that Scion as it is, was made as a limited game, they never intended it to go past the first 3 books but added the 2 additional books (Companion and Ragnarok) due to overwhelming fan interest....and I can only assume the Yazata file was put together for the same reason, though if you look through it the meat of it was the important part to get out as unlike the other books, they spent exactly 0 hours on the art (Look through the other books and you'll find that, unless I missed something, every single picture in that file is from another book). It is a new company that is starting over and are, I am assuming here, looking to expand past the limited line into the ability to continue the game further on down the road. So in all honesty instead of looking at it as a 2nd Edition, you can really look at it as a Remake.</div> </div> </div> </div>As best I can tell, the Yazata pantheon pic is original - I haven't seen it elsewhere in Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T08:49:12-07:00","id":282335,"title":"","content":"Ah yeah, forgot about the Pantheon pic itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T09:05:07-07:00","id":283905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=276592#post276592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A second edition of CtL is already in the works, actually, so that's probably a good call.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the heads-up.<br /> <br /> I hadn't heard that.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T09:32:25-07:00","id":283917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=275578#post275578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another reason is that they're artists, of a sort, and it's been about 15 years since they've made art on this subject. They want to be creative and bring new art into the world, so they're making new art.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfectly understandable. I guess I'm just not a fan of applying gesso to cover a prior masterpiece and paint the new masterpiece right on top of it. That is what these new editions (of any company and any game) are starting to feel like to me...not an expansion of the art, but a covering of existing art to display new art.<br /> <br /> But this is my issue to deal with. I think my question was answered and thanks to the powers that be.<br /> <br /> I was wanting to know if these were vast setting changes or just rules tweaks while building on the past releases and I believe I have my answers for these games.<br /> <br /> Now I have the hard personal choices to make. Replace the books and settings that I bought and loved with the new creations...or continue to enjoy the massive library I've already built up. If I do the latter, then I'll have my disposable funds to put into truly new games and settings as they are released instead of deciding to dump the old to make way for the new.<br /> <br /> Only time will tell which way I go.<br /> <br /> But thanks again everyone for the discourse to help that decision.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T13:19:08-07:00","id":286123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MidnightBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=273891#post273891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. Like I said, it wasn't a &quot;which is better&quot; discussion. I really was just trying to gauge if we were talking rules change, setting change, or both.<br /> <br /> But the argument that, &quot;It's been X years since the book came out so we need to make a new one,&quot; does rub me a little wrong.<br /> <br /> The classics never die...well...until someone stops printing the books and they become impossible to grab. =)</div> </div> </div> </div>They just told you. They lack the files.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MidnightBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=273891#post273891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand having a new vision for a concept and wanting to make a new game to take the game to new places.<br /> <br /> I can understand trying to alter the feel of a game with new mechanics.<br /> <br /> But I never really understood the notion that if something hasn't been altered in 5, 10, 20, or even 30+ years, then it is outdated.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 1E doesn't really do it for me, it never really did after I discovered more free form advancement and build systems, but it sure seems to work well for others...even after all these years.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what a shame if they had stopped and not given us AD&amp;D or 1st edition Champions had not led to 5th edition Hero System.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MidnightBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=273891#post273891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to keep my eye on the progress of these three games/settings and see if I'll jump in. I HAVE to stop somewhere and just enjoy what I have. A new supplement can build on existing campaigns...even years and decades old. A new system might allow for a conversion, but sometimes is just far too much trouble than it is worth. But that's something that I'll need to evaluate on my own side of the screen.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the insight all.<br /> <br /> =)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing to stop you from using stuff from the old books with a little rework. Also The Galeata exploded in 1998. The Timeline could use some retweaking.<br /> And Dude, there has been @ least 30 years of super hero gaming. How many Superhero systems have been released since then.<br /> What can be learned from them?<br /> This is Onyx Paths chance to survey the field and see what they feel works and hasn't worked from various lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","user":"Chattnos","date":". 10-18-2014, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T09:00:43-07:00","id":286665,"title":"","content":"As you've said Chattnos, all of that had been long answered, but thanks for your 2 bits anyway.<br /> <br /> Never quite sure why people seem to take offense at honest inquiries, but sorry if I hurt a feeling there somewhere.<br /> <br /> I've been a gamer for a long time and I've seen a lot of new versions of a book come out.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it is only the rules that change. Sometimes drastically and sometimes just little tweaks that a FAQ could have handled.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it is the entire concept that changes...the flavor, the major parties, the whole setting. Sometimes it is just an expansion of the timeline...the old book was the setting 10 years in the past, the new book is &quot;now&quot;.<br /> <br /> I was simply trying to gauge where these revisions of books I already own fall into those spectrums.<br /> <br /> In a perfect world, I'd buy them all.<br /> <br /> It's not a perfect world. Despite a good income and a huge game room lined with bookcases, I've come to the point where I have to make hard choices. What gets replaced? What goes to the basement? What finally prompts me to try to sell something on Ebay instead of just buy?<br /> <br /> This is where I'm at.<br /> <br /> With the books that are getting ready to go into 2nd Editions that I was asking about, I already have pretty much everything that has been put out for them in the 1st Edition...and I've loved those books and games.<br /> <br /> If these 2nd Editions were simply an expansion on the well written books that I already loved, then it would be a no brainer...gotta buy.<br /> <br /> If these are starting from the ground up, ignoring everything that had come before in the books that I already own and love, then they are just going to have to really be over and above good to find a spot on my shelves and get me to remove what is already there. I'm not saying these authors can't do that. But in my case they have an uphill battle (not that it needs to mean a lick to them). Because they aren't just trying to wow me with a cool and original concept (like the Demon the Descent as 50's Cold War-esque intrigue). No, they have to sell me on why their concept of a Promethean is better than the concept of a Promethean that I've already invested so much time, love, and money into.<br /> <br /> This is where I find myself in life right now, and why I asked the questions that I did.<br /> <br /> As I've said from the beginning...in no way was this meant as an edition war debate. I simply needed to know what &quot;2nd Edition&quot; meant in the specific cases of each of these books.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all of the answers directed at the intent of the post.<br /> <br /> It has been most helpful.<br /> <br /> I love everything I have from White-Wolf and Onyx Path. Thanks for decades of fun!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T09:09:09-07:00","id":287714,"title":"","content":"The purpose of a second edition isn't just to update things - though, that's a big part of it. When Aberrant was originally published, reality TV hadn't yet hit the heights it would, and we certainly didn't have the Kardashians. <br /> <br /> Nor is it to holistically incorporate what's come up in supplements into the core game experience - though that's a big part too. You mention Promethean, but the Second Edition has the various sourcebook Lineages and Refinements as part of core gameplay.<br /> <br /> If those were simple date changes or copy paste jobs, yeah, I can see your issue. But another edition is a full refocus of the line's themes, mechanics, and play experience. In Trinity's case, it's a way to reconcile and enrich all three games by interlinking them, rather than having winks and nods in the books. Demon the Descent isn't a different take on Demon the Fallen - it's drawing on similar source material to create a whole new game. Politics on a space station? Babylon 5 and DS9. Second Edition? Battlestar Galactica and nuBSG. <br /> <br /> And no, we won't take your books away. But the second edition is a chance to more deeply and fully explore some themes the first editions didn't get around to (for many reasons) while refocusing the core play experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T11:59:29-07:00","id":288732,"title":"","content":"It's gonna be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T15:02:54-07:00","id":288983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=287714#post287714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Aberrant was originally published, reality TV hadn't yet hit the heights it would, and we certainly didn't have the Kardashians.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, happy days....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T23:11:42-07:00","id":289285,"title":"","content":"Also Aberrant's presentation of global politics was very very much a post-Cold War, pre-9/11 American narrative - that is to say, it shows that it was written in the period in which there was a sense of American/Western/Neo-Liberal invulnerability and omnipotence on the world stage... at least for Americans. I mean in some ways it deconstructed that myth of ascending peace under the neo-liberal social order - but that myth itself is outdated at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-22-2014, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T03:44:41-07:00","id":289396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=289285#post289285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Aberrant's presentation of global politics was very very much a post-Cold War, pre-9/11 American narrative - that is to say, it shows that it was written in the period in which there was a sense of American/Western/Neo-Liberal invulnerability and omnipotence on the world stage... at least for Americans. I mean in some ways it deconstructed that myth of ascending peace under the neo-liberal social order - but that myth itself is outdated at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It did predict the outsourcing of military operations to ever smaller numbers of special forces and local proxies rather than full scale direct involvement. Granted Seals and guerillas don't wear tights and air strike isn't necessarily the same thing as compact car tossed into low orbit on a ballistic trajectory....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T08:47:22-07:00","id":289627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=288983#post288983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, happy days....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now THAT I can agree with and get behind!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3194-midnightblue","name":"MidnightBlue","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T12:26:23-07:00","id":289880,"title":"","content":"DISCLAIMER: Everything that follows is armchair anthropology.<br /> <br /> Just to echo what Neall and glamourweaver are saying: popular culture has changed between then and now. <br /> <br /> At the time that Aberrant came out, I'm pretty sure things like DC's Kingdom Come--relatively fresh in the cultural mindset at a mere 3 years old--were well-etched into its DNA. Culturally, I suppose we were in a good spot: we'd come out ahead in the Cold War, the economy was ridiculously robust, and gas was commonly under a dollar. I think it's fair to say we knew it was too good to last: this is the era of X-Files and Fight Club, after all. And Neall points out that the concept of reality TV celebrity hadn't really clicked yet. Sure, the Real World had been around a while, but it was fairly novel (Survivor wouldn't be for another year) and if it was imitated at the time, its competitors haven't lingered in my memory.<br /> <br /> Fast forward to the present day. On the comics front, we have Civil War looming in our rear view mirror, which I expect to cast a dark shadow over the idea of registered superheroes, while culturally the never-ending war on terror stretches ahead of us (hello drones), and reality TV is a terrifying and inescapable juggernaut: even though I've never watched an episode of the Kardashians, I could name more than one of them. Some of the things that might have seemed like possibly dystopian extrapolations fifteen years ago are now things that, in one way or another, we've seen. They're real.<br /> <br /> It behooves any game to tap into the zeitgeist into which it's released in its moods and themes, especially one that hovers around the modern day and/or very near future, like Aberrant does. There are some similarities, obviously between then and now, but I expect when I pick up the second edition, there's going to be a moment where I look at a turn of phrase or the presentation of a setting element and go, &quot;...yeah, this is definitely something that wouldn't have been written in the first edition.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T13:43:14-07:00","id":290754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cowardly Scion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/272992-why-a-second-edition?p=289396#post289396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It did predict the outsourcing of military operations to ever smaller numbers of special forces and local proxies rather than full scale direct involvement. Granted Seals and guerillas don't wear tights and air strike isn't necessarily the same thing as compact car tossed into low orbit on a ballistic trajectory....</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that idea has been around for some time - i remember at least <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_America_%28film%29\" target=\"_blank\">one movie</a> that scratched the issue back in the early 90's, set during and parallel to the Vietnam War to boot, though it's quite true the phenomenon wasn't very well known before the Iraq War's stormy years of occupation or more precisely the Blackwater controversy almost a decade after Aberrant.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now speaking of editions &amp; stuff - everyone has their preferences for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> - Played Star Wars with D6 and still play and ST with a tweaked version of it, though i tried D20 and admit their Force mechanics were better balanced with the whole system and keep a module or two for reference. Though curious about Edge of Empire never touched even one book of the Fantasy Flight version.<br /> <br /> - Started in Storyteller with 1e Masquerade, lost interest late in 2nd edition's run, utterly ignored 3rd because i hated the creative directions though the mechanics seemed pretty slick and cleaned up. V20 got me some nostalgia and involved in the VtM forums and writing some stuff again on a lark (though i have yet to actually make a group and ST, i've played it a little online).<br /> <br /> - Felt none too certain about Requiem - and actually expected to dislike it as much if not more than VtM's late run - but against my own expectations, found much to love in the directions taken with Requiem, fell in and never really looked back and, V20 tinkering notwithstanding, still mostly play it (updating to Blood &amp; Smoke slow, by bits and pieces, as the mood strikes the group).<br /> <br /> - Supers games, i have played lots of them through the years - Champions, Heroes Unlimited, Villains &amp; Vigilantes, DC Heroes, MSH, DC Universe, Marvel (Saga Edition), Aberrant...in fact the super hero games were what attracted me to RPGs and appealed to me on a level D&amp;D and other Tolkien derivatives never really matched. And yet while i have tried M&amp;M, Necessary Evil (Savage Worlds) and some other, newer games targeting the genre, none haven't appealed to me like those older ones did. Most &quot;modern&quot; hero games i have played were homebrewed experiments/adaptations with Scion, nWoD and Exalted, in ascending order of success. Read Orpheus years after the closed series/setting was over but became a fan, got all books and made an Aberrant timeline of my own strongly inspired by elements and events of the series.<br /> <br /> - Never really got into Trinity (nothing against it, simply didn't get my attention attracted to it), but Aberrant and Adventure i love with a passion (even though i never really played or STed the last one) and have played more than one chronicle and spin-off out of it, love the setting and the systems both, each with its pros, cons and homebrews.<br /> <br /> That said, we have had more than one and a half decade of evolving variants of the Storyteller games (Exalted, nWoD, Scion, cWoD 20th anniversary editions, God-Machine nWoD) and increasing success of the genre in a number of media (Batman of the Future in '99-'01, X-Men: Evolution in '01-03, JLA &amp; JLA: Unlimited from '01-'06, Teen Titans in '03-06, the Spider-man movies, X-men movies, Nolan's Batman trilogy, Marvel Studios cinematic 'verse, that now also includes Guardians of the Galaxy, the adventure/space opera film of the year. Can any of these many influences, of system or media - and lots of stuff produced in these years that i did not mention (no Lord of Rings, Sin City, Avatar the Last Airbender (cartoon), Narnia or Harry Potter movies back then<b>*</b>) - add, change or bring novel elements to the system, setting and its portrayal?<br /> <br /> <b>*</b>No Twilight either - in that i really envy the luck of our past selves...<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe, maybe not, honestly, i have no idea whatsoever for certain and i find this <b>good</b> for once - last time i ever saw someone talking of the game was that utterly awful D20 version or some campaign nostalgia in some blog i forget. Fans have crawled out of the darkest recesses of the net and are discussing coming books and stuff about games old and new, not to mention the occasional experiment some, like me, did in the silent years. There's curiosity, doubt, expectation and a sense of wonder &amp; surprise about the incoming game(s) and i for one find it very good and much better than trying to get echo out of the limbo. These blurbs in particular had me salivating i won't lie:<ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">One writer's biggest inspirations were the TV shows Continuum and Fringe.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Important distinction - &quot;Trinity Continuum&quot;, not Trinity Universe. The Continuum has a unique relationship with quantum mechanics and time travel, inherent in the way dramatic editing works within the setting. It adds an extra weight to Aberrant and Trinity's assertion that, &quot;no, the future needn't go this way.&quot;</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> There's change coming, for good and for ill, but we will have new material to pore over, discuss, criticize, use, mine for ideas or burn at the streets in rage &amp; disgust (like sometimes i wish i had done with my Kindred of the East...). Let it come and us all be judges of it when the game(s) is actually out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-24-2014, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}